model g13_spacing
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.6 (#81, P21), G13: L §2.4 The loader accepts any spacing the grammar allows: a record field spaced at its . (pair .x, pair. y, pair . x), an id at its [ (added [q2], an item named as a calendar list word), a call at its ( (max (…)) read as written touching, and a keyword keeps its space before ( (not (…)). refcore 2.1.5 refused the spaced field (LOAD-PARSE). Its twin, the same text touching, answers the same."

source plan "T's invented plan"

index qs = [q1, q2]

input pair: (x int, y int)

input added[k in qs]: int

input base: int

def fields: int = pair .x + pair. y + pair . x

def keyed: int = added [q2] + max (base, added [q1])

def kept: bool = not (base > pair.y or base < added[q2])

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pair = (x: 4, y: 9)
  added[q1] = 7
  added[q2] = 2
  base = 3

ask q: fields, keyed, kept
